SUMMARY:Cookbook Swap & Baked Goods Tasting
DESCRIPTION:Join us for another Cookbook Swap! \nCookbook Swap: 10:30 AM–1:30 PM | Café Area\nBaked Goods Tasting: 12:00–1:30 PM | Auditorium \nBring your gently used cookbooks and exchange them 1-for-1 with fellow culinary enthusiasts. Maximum of 5 books. \nDrop off your cookbooks at the library in advance\, prior to October 10. \nOn the day of the event\, for every cookbook you’ve donated\, you’ll get to choose a new one to take home!\nAnd this time\, we’re adding something delicious! You can bring a homemade baked good for fellow cookbook lovers to sample and enjoy. Please bring your baked good ready to serve—there will be no heating\, reheating\, or cooking of food at the event. Bringing a baked good is completely optional—you’re welcome to attend the cookbook swap and bake-off even if you don’t bring food. \nIf you plan to bring a baked good\, please email adultprograms@montclairlibrary.org and let us know what you will be bringing. All baked goods must be nut-free. \nPlease note: Baked goods may contain other common allergens\, and the library cannot guarantee an allergen-free environment or be responsible for allergic reactions or other food-related sensitivities. Please use your best judgment when sampling foods. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/cookbook-swap-baked-goods-tasting/
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library\, 50 South Fullerton Avenue\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Food,Literature
