DESCRIPTION:Director: Catalina Beltrán\nPlaywright: Naomi Iizuka \nIn Polaroid Stories (play) by Naomi Iizuka\, young people gather in an abandoned mansion where myth and the present collide\, revealing cycles of power\, loss\, and survival. \nDirector Statement:\nSet in a decaying mansion once built to project authority\, this production focuses on those living at the margins and the systems that shape their lives. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
