SUMMARY:Festival de los Andes at Montclair State University (Rain date)
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Montclair State University for the Festival de los Andes\, a vibrant\, family-friendly celebration of the cultures and Indigenous traditions of the Andean region. Experience an afternoon of live music and dance\, artists and artisans\, interactive cultural workshops\, food\, family activities\, and more\, with performances and traditions representing Colombia\, Ecuador\, Peru\, Bolivia\, and Argentina.\nThis year’s expanded festival features 12 performing groups and a special Women’s Voices program bringing together singers representing Colombia\, Ecuador\, Bolivia\, and Peru. More than a festival\, it is a space for the University and surrounding communities to come together through culture\, learning\, connection\, and celebration.\nFree and open to the community.\nPlease note: The Festival was originally scheduled for September 26 and has been rescheduled to October 10 due to inclement weather. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
