SUMMARY:Lunatic Fringe Improv Comedy Show 30th Season Opener!
DESCRIPTION:Lunatic Fringe\, New Jersey’s longest running improv troupe\, launches its 30th season with a show at the Glen Ridge Train Station (Community Center) at 8 p.m. on October 10th. \nIt’s not deep. It’s rarely thought-provoking. It’s just funny! \nThe group uses music and audience suggestions to create a show that’s different every time\, but always funny – and always apolitical! \nLunatic Fringe performers include Director Deb Maclean\, Paul Murphy\, Dave Groveman\, and Gary Van Lieu. Ben Rausch improvises on piano. \nThe show is suitable for older children\, and you are welcome to bring your own refreshments. \nTickets are still only $12 at the door\, but with a reservation\, admission is only $10. Cash only. For reservations\, CALL (973) 429-1527. (Texting not possible.) \nCheck out our article in NJ Monthly! https://njmonthly.com/articles/arts-entertainment/lunatic-fringe-wacky-nj-improv-group-centers-audience-suggestions/ \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/lunatic-fringe-improv-comedy-show-30th-season-opener/2026-10-10/
